      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "#1975 turns `ctime_tests` back on for ARM64, where no CI job has run them since #1689. It does not touch ARM32, which this issue is about.\n\nI ran `ctime_tests` under Valgrind 3.24 on Linux aarch64 with gcc 14 and clang 19: at the default settings, with window 2 and gen-kb 2, at -O1 and at -O3. All passed. With a branch on `high` in `secp256k1_ecdsa_sig_sign`, both compilers failed. The host cannot run 32-bit ARM code, so this says nothing about the ARM32 assembly. Logs on request.\n",
